            <title>[LU-21080] sanity-sec test_27c: NULL pointer dereference in ping_evictor_main</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21080</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-sec test_27c: the server node crashed with a NULL pointer dereference in ping_evictor_main (ll_evictor thread), CR2 = 0000000000000030.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Config: review-dne-zfs-part-2, el10.1 ZFS servers (6.12.0-124.56.1.el10_1_lustre), master 43a09f028a (2.17.60_73), session 0572e44c-4787-43a2-ade7-95c8622c84a9, node onyx-141vm40.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Console log:&lt;br/&gt;
BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 0000000000000030&lt;br/&gt;
RIP: 0010:ping_evictor_main+0x1a6/0x8c0 &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;ptlrpc&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Comm: ll_evictor&lt;br/&gt;
Call Trace: ping_evictor_main &amp;lt; kthread &amp;lt; ret_from_fork&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The faulting load is obd-&amp;gt;obd_type-&amp;gt;typ_name (the LUSTRE_OSP_NAME strcmp) right after list_first_entry(&amp;amp;pet_list, ...). R13 holds the address of pet_list itself, so the pet_list was empty when the thread took its first entry: obd was derived from the list head and obd_type read as NULL. The loop only waits for a non-empty list or PET_TERMINATE, and ping_evictor_main() is the only place that removes entries, so the list was emptied (or the state flipped) between the wait and the first-entry read, for example two evictor threads alive across a ptlrpc ping_evictor_stop()/start() cycle (the node had reloaded ptlrpc several times earlier in the session). The code is not touched by the tested patch (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;, change 69392); the crash happened in sanity-sec while the earlier sanity-lfsck test_2e had also logged an unrelated osd_index_it_key memcpy field-spanning WARN.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frequency: test_27c failed 2 of 2369 review-dne-zfs-part-2 runs since 2026-10-01 (one CRASH, one TIMEOUT); no existing LU ticket mentions ping_evictor_main with a NULL dereference (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18669" title="sanity-sec test_27c hung" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18669"&gt;LU-18669&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18569" title="sanity-sec: timeout - clients lost connection to MGS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18569"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18569&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are Autotest timeouts of this test).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suggested fix: in ping_evictor_main() recheck list_empty(&amp;amp;pet_list) under pet_lock before list_first_entry() and continue the loop when empty.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps3-7a5fd9b84a77 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
